  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Groups should have a more reliable way to see who performed moderation actions, such as bans, kicks, and warnings, when viewing a user’s history. Right now, this information can become unavailable if the group logs do not go back far enough, which creates confusion for staff trying to understand past actions or decisions.\n\nWhen a moderator looks up a user who has previously been moderated, the system should clearly show what action was taken, who performed it, when it happened, and the reason if one was given. This information should be stored in a way that does not rely on standard log history, so it remains accessible at all times.\n\nHaving this available would make it easier for staff to understand past decisions and prevent situations where actions cannot be traced back to the person who made them.",
